 "review": {
  "score": 5.0,
  "round": 1,
  "problems": [
   "Doesn't read as a spiral conch at a glance. The body is a jagged, faceted 12-point polygon with no stepped, tapering spire. In the person and wide views it reads as a croissant or a leaf-shaped lump.",
   "The body curves at (-70..30, -168..-40) all fan out from the top-left corner, so they look like leaf veins or ribs, not spiral seams. No whorls are visible.",
   "The pointed tip is just a blunt corner with a gold dot at (-92,-168), so the shell has no pointed end.",
   "The lip at (32..110, -176..-36) is a hard hexagon pasted onto the side like a pink plate. It doesn't curve out from the body, so it doesn't read as a flared lip.",
   "No siphonal canal (the narrow tapered spout at the base), which helps a conch silhouette read.",
   "Spikes stand up in a straight row like a crown instead of following the curve of the shoulder."
  ]
 },
 "for": "Giant spiral conch shell on a sandy mound. The diver blows it to summon the dolphins, so it is the story's focal prop. Pearly pink-cream interior and a flared l",
